<section class="container py-4 policy-document">

    <h1>Donation Policy</h1>

    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> 8 September 2026</p>

    <p>
        Voice of Ex-Servicemen is committed to maintaining transparency and
        accountability in receiving and utilising donations. This Donation Policy
        explains the terms and conditions applicable to donations made through our
        website.
    </p>

    <h4>1. Acceptance of Donations</h4>

    <p>
        Voice of Ex-Servicemen accepts voluntary donations from individuals and
        organisations through the payment methods made available on our website.
        Donations are intended to support activities and initiatives consistent
        with the aims and objectives of the organisation.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Voluntary Contributions</h2>

    <p>
        All donations made through this website are voluntary contributions.
        Donors are requested to carefully review the donation amount and payment
        details before completing a transaction.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Online Payment Processing</h2>

    <p>
        Online donations may be processed through third-party payment gateways
        and payment service providers. Voice of Ex-Servicemen does not request
        or directly store sensitive payment credentials such as debit card PINs,
        credit card CVVs, UPI PINs, passwords, or internet banking passwords.
    </p>

    <p>
        Payment transactions are subject to the terms, conditions and privacy
        policies of the relevant payment gateway, bank, card network, UPI service
        provider, or other financial institution involved in the transaction.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Donation Confirmation</h2>

    <p>
        A donation will be considered successfully received after the transaction
        has been successfully processed and the corresponding amount has been
        credited to the organisation or otherwise confirmed through the applicable
        payment system.
    </p>

    <p>
        Where applicable, a donation acknowledgement or receipt may be sent to
        the email address or other contact details provided by the donor.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Failed or Incomplete Transactions</h2>

    <p>
        If a transaction fails or is cancelled before the donation is successfully
        received by the organisation, the donation will not be considered completed.
    </p>

    <p>
        If a donor's bank account or payment instrument has been debited but the
        organisation has not received the corresponding amount, the donor may
        contact us with the relevant transaction details so that the transaction
        can be verified.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Use of Donations</h2>

    <p>
        Donations may be used to support activities consistent with the aims and
        objectives of Voice of Ex-Servicemen, including welfare activities,
        awareness programmes, assistance initiatives, advocacy, organisational
        activities, and reasonable administrative and operational expenses.
    </p>

    <p>
        Unless a specific purpose has been expressly accepted by the organisation,
        donations may be utilised according to the organisation's current
        priorities and requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Donor Information</h2>

    <p>
        Information collected during the donation process will be handled in
        accordance with our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Tax Receipts and Benefits</h2>

    <p>
        Where applicable, donation receipts or other relevant documentation may
        be issued in accordance with the organisation's status, eligibility and
        applicable laws.
    </p>

    <p>
        Donors are responsible for providing accurate information required for
        the issuance of any receipt or applicable documentation.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Fraudulent or Unauthorised Transactions</h2>

    <p>
        Voice of Ex-Servicemen reserves the right to investigate transactions that
        appear to be fraudulent, unauthorised, suspicious, or otherwise irregular.
        Where necessary, such matters may be referred to the relevant payment
        service provider, bank, or competent authority.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>

    <p>
        We may update this Donation Policy from time to time. Any changes will
        be published on this page along with the revised effective date.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>

    <p>
        For questions regarding donations, payment transactions, receipts, or
        this Donation Policy, please contact us through our
        <a href="/contact-us/">Contact Us</a> page.
    </p>

    </section>